findings.actual:
- DialogInput.swift:191-199 calls library.attachSubtitle for every episode, which becomes VLC_ML_MEDIA_ADD_EXTERNAL_MRL (MXRLibraryServices.m:319). Only the episode playing right now also gets addExternalTrack.
- Nothing reads those media-library files back:
  - the bridge's media conversion reads only VLC_ML_FILE_TYPE_MAIN (MXRLibraryServices.m:19-20);
  - VLCQueueBackend.wireItem (VLCQueueBackend.swift:47-55) adds only track-preference options;
  - queueCommand (MXRServicesBridge.m:688-710) adds no slaves;
  - VLC core's src/player/medialib.c restores position and track ids, but not external files.
- So when the next episode starts, the subtitle the user just matched is not loaded, and External Tracks is empty. This is the core promise of §06. It needs runtime confirmation with a two-episode folder.
